  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 145 PM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nThursday through Tuesday:\n\nThe west to east surface ridge will continue to reside from the\nnrn Great Lakes to srn Quebec through Fri nt. This will maintain\nrelatively cool ely winds and high relative humidity over srn\nWI. Lows in the 40s and 50s and highs in the middle to upper 60s\nare forecast. The srn periphery of a shortwave trough moving\nacross Ontario may traverse across central and srn WI Thu\nafternoon and night but only mid to high clouds are expected at\nthis time. \n\nA narrow upper ridge will then build into the region for Fri-Fri nt\nfollowed by a weak and slow moving shortwave trough that will attempt\nto run through the ridge over WI for Sat nt-Sun. Rain chances are\n20-40 percent over south central WI Sat nt, then 20 percent on \nSun. Upper ridging and warming temps will then return for early \nnext week. However, 30-40 percent chances for showers are \nforecast on Tue when the upper ridge shifts ewd. \n\nGehring",
